"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers some central content: written policies governing basket construction and acceptance, detailed custom-basket parameters tied to the best interests of the fund and shareholders, and documentation of each custom basket and its policy compliance. It has several substantive omissions and errors. (1) It omits the required process for revising or departing from custom-basket policies. (2) For review roles, it describes board oversight and generic compliance and portfolio-management duties. It does not state the requirement to identify the titles or roles of adviser employees who review each custom basket for compliance. (3) It omits that records must show a basket's custom status. (4) Its custom-basket definition is incomplete. It says only that a custom basket 'differs in composition from the standard basket'. The rule's two prongs are a basket not representative of the fund's holdings, or a representative basket that differs from the initial basket used that business day. (5) It characterizes a non-standard order as a deviation in terms within an otherwise standard basket. This does not capture the key point that custom-basket status is a regulatory classification distinct from contractual approval of a non-standard order. Useful core content with multiple material gaps supports 'partial'.\"}","ttft_ms":3050,"type":"result","duration_ms":6810,"uuid":"79f30213-8545-4ab6-b5ef-ef37088a416d","ttft_stream_ms":553,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":554,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
